    },
    {
      "type": "figure",
      "id": "fig-00001",
      "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
      "caption": null,
      "media": {
        "alt": {
          "segmentId": "m00338:alt:fig-00001-alt",
          "text": "Alpha-amino acids are demaninated to  alpha-keto acids and ammonia. The alpha-keto acids enter the Citric Acid cycle and converted into pyruvate, oxaloacetate, alpha-ketoglutarate, succinyl CoA fumarate acetoacetate or acetyl CoA."
        },
        "src": "../../media/OChem_29_09_001.jpg",
        "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "section",
      "id": "sect-00001",
      "class": null,
      "title": {
        "segmentId": "m00338:title:sect-00001-title",
        "text": "Transamination"
      },
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00002",
          "segmentId": "m00338:para:para-00002"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00002",
          "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
          "caption": null,
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00338:alt:fig-00002-alt",
              "text": "Alpha-amino acid reacts with alpha-ketoglutarate in the presence of pyridoxal phosphate to form an alpha-keto acid, glutamate. The square parentheses below show pyridoxal phosphate and pyridoxine."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_29_09_002.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "para",
          "id": "para-00003",
          "segmentId": "m00338:para:para-00003"
        },
        {
          "type": "figure",
          "id": "fig-00003",
          "class": "mechanism-figure scaled-down",
          "caption": {
            "segmentId": "m00338:caption:fig-00003-caption"
          },
          "media": {
            "alt": {
              "segmentId": "m00338:alt:fig-00003-alt",
              "text": "Enzymatic catalyzed deamination of an alpha amino acid to form an alpha-keto acid and pyridoxamine phosphate."
            },
            "src": "../../media/OChem_29_09_003.jpg",
            "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00002",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00338:title:sect-00002-title",
            "text": "Step 1 of [[xref:fig-00003]]: Transimination"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00004",
              "segmentId": "m00338:para:para-00004"
            },
            {
              "type": "figure",
              "id": "fig-00004",
              "class": "unnumbered scaled-down",
              "caption": null,
              "media": {
                "alt": {
                  "segmentId": "m00338:alt:fig-00004-alt",
                  "text": "An enzyme-bound PLP-amino acid imine reacts with an amino acid to provide a diamine intermediate which decomposes to a PlP-amino acid imine and the free amino enzyme."
                },
                "src": "../../media/OChem_29_09_004.jpg",
                "mimeType": "image/jpeg"
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "section",
          "id": "sect-00003",
          "class": null,
          "title": {
            "segmentId": "m00338:title:sect-00003-title",
            "text": "Steps 2–4 of [[xref:fig-00003]]: Tautomerization and Hydrolysis"
          },
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "para",
              "id": "para-00005",
